IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-s5-definitions`

-- Hand-written tests for the section 5 terms a person with a time limit or a notice is most likely to meet.
-- Every expected value is written from the text of section 5 (lines 128 to 256 of the raw text), not from the table.

§ `Tests -- section 5, key terms`

-- parent includes three kinds of person; "includes" does not shut out others, so an unlisted person gets no answer.
#ASSERT `the way section 5 defines the word` "parent" EQUALS JUST `it includes`
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "parent" "a person who is an adoptive parent under the Adoption Act 1994" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "parent" "a person who is a parent within the meaning of the Artificial Conception Act 1985" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "parent" "a person who is a parent in a relationship of parent and child that arises because of a parentage order under the Surrogacy Act 2008" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "parent" "a foster carer" EQUALS NOTHING

-- person includes a public body, a company, and an association or body of persons, corporate or unincorporate.
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "person" "a company" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "person" "a public body" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "person" "an association or body of persons, corporate or unincorporate" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "person" "a trust" EQUALS NOTHING
-- individual means a natural person.
#ASSERT `the way section 5 defines the word` "individual" EQUALS JUST `it means`

-- sell includes barter, exchange, offer to sell and expose for sale.
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "sell" "barter" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "sell" "exchange" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "sell" "offer to sell" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "sell" "expose for sale" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "sell" "give away" EQUALS NOTHING

-- sign includes the affixing or making of a seal, mark or thumbprint.
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "sign" "thumbprint" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "sign" "mark" EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- year and financial year are twelve-month periods (the dates are in wa-interpretation-time.l4); month is defined by s 62.
#ASSERT `the way section 5 defines the word` "year" EQUALS JUST `it means`
#ASSERT `the way section 5 defines the word` "financial year" EQUALS JUST `it means`
#ASSERT `the way section 5 defines the word` "month" EQUALS JUST `its meaning is given elsewhere`
#ASSERT `the provision that gives the meaning of the word` "month" EQUALS JUST "section 62"
#ASSERT `the provision that gives the meaning of the word` "year" EQUALS NOTHING

-- Meanings given by another provision of this Act or by another Act.
#ASSERT `the provision that gives the meaning of the word` "bankrupt" EQUALS JUST "section 13D"
#ASSERT `the provision that gives the meaning of the word` "death" EQUALS JUST "section 13C"
#ASSERT `the provision that gives the meaning of the word` "de facto relationship" EQUALS JUST "section 13A"
#ASSERT `the provision that gives the meaning of the word` "local government district" EQUALS JUST "section 13CA"
#ASSERT `the provision that gives the meaning of the word` "Minister" EQUALS JUST "section 12"
#ASSERT `the provision that gives the meaning of the word` "rules of court" EQUALS JUST "section 66"
#ASSERT `the provision that gives the meaning of the word` "indictable offence" EQUALS JUST "section 67"
#ASSERT `the provision that gives the meaning of the word` "simple offence" EQUALS JUST "section 67"
#ASSERT `the provision that gives the meaning of the word` "WA legislation website" EQUALS JUST "the Legislation Act 2021 section 8(1)"

-- Names that share one definition are found under either name.
#ASSERT `the way section 5 defines the word` "this State" EQUALS JUST `it means`
#ASSERT `the way section 5 defines the word` "the State" EQUALS JUST `it means`
#ASSERT `the way section 5 defines the word` "JP" EQUALS JUST `it means`
#ASSERT `the way section 5 defines the word` "King" EQUALS JUST `it means and includes`
#ASSERT `the way section 5 defines the word` "Government Gazette" EQUALS JUST `it means`
#ASSERT `the way section 5 defines the word` "de facto partner" EQUALS JUST `its meaning is given elsewhere`

-- act (small a) and Act (capital A) are two different entries.
#ASSERT `the way section 5 defines the word` "act" EQUALS JUST `it includes`
#ASSERT `the way section 5 defines the word` "Act" EQUALS JUST `it means`
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "act" "an omission" EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Closed lists: "means" over named things shuts out the rest.
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "Australia Acts" "the Australia Act 1986 of the Commonwealth" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "Australia Acts" "the Australia Act 1986 of the United Kingdom" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "Australia Acts" "the Australia Act 1986 of New Zealand" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "court of summary jurisdiction" "the Children’s Court" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "court of summary jurisdiction" "the Magistrates Court" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "court of summary jurisdiction" "the District Court" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "written law" "all Acts for the time being in force" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "written law" "a Bill before Parliament" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "enactment" "any portion of a written law" EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- subsidiary legislation lists its kinds, but ends with "or other instrument", so an unlisted kind is not shut out.
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "subsidiary legislation" "notice" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "subsidiary legislation" "local law" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "subsidiary legislation" "circular" EQUALS NOTHING

-- under includes by, in accordance with, pursuant to and by virtue of.
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "under" "pursuant to" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "under" "by virtue of" EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- repeal, amend, penalty, writing, words.
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "repeal" "revoke" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "amend" "vary" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "amend" "abolish" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "penalty" "imprisonment" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "writing" "photocopying" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "words" "symbols" EQUALS JUST TRUE
